Bundled third-party components
------------------------------
* JCodec 0.2.5 — https://jcodec.org/ — FreeBSD (BSD 2-Clause) License.
  Embedded in the released jar as META-INF/jarjar/jcodec-0.2.5.jar (via NeoForge jarJar).
  Used by the video converter (MP4/H.264 -> MJPEG).
* Audio decoders, used **only** by the music widget (see "Music module" below).
  They are embedded unmodified as separate jars in META-INF/jarjar/ and can be
  replaced individually, which is what the LGPL permits for a work that uses the library:
  - mp3spi 1.9.5.4, jlayer 1.0.1.4, tritonus-share 0.3.7.4 (MP3)
    — JavaZOOM, GNU LGPL 2.1. https://www.javazoom.net/
  - jflac-codec 1.5.3 (FLAC) — Josh Coalson / jFLAC project, BSD-style license.
  None of these libraries are modified, and none of their source is copied into
  this project's own source tree.
* Optional runtime interop with WaterMedia (https://modrinth.com/mod/watermedia):
  no source code, classes or binaries from that project are used, compiled against or
  bundled. When it happens to be installed, this mod calls its publicly documented API
  by reflection (name lookup at runtime) so its decoders can play common video formats.
  WaterMedia is licensed under PolyForm Strict 1.0.0, which is not compatible with this
  project's Apache-2.0; keeping the dependency optional and reflective is deliberate.
* Fonts shipped in assets/projector/font/ (minecraft.ttf, caviar_dreams.ttf)
